      "originalText": "Greet one another with a holy kiss. All the churches of Christ greet you⁺.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.16.17",
      "sourceRef": "ROM.16.17",
      "sourceId": "blb.txt#line=28357",
      "sourceLabel": "17",
      "anchors": [
        "ROM.16.17"
      ],
      "mappingType": "exact",
      "text": "Now I exhort you⁺, brothers, to watch out for those causing divisions and obstacles contrary to the teaching that you⁺ learned, and turn away from them.",
      "originalText": "Now I exhort you⁺, brothers, to watch out for those causing divisions and obstacles contrary to the teaching that you⁺ learned, and turn away from them.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.16.18",
      "sourceRef": "ROM.16.18",
      "sourceId": "blb.txt#line=28358",
      "sourceLabel": "18",
      "anchors": [
        "ROM.16.18"
      ],
      "mappingType": "exact",
      "text": "For such do not serve our Lord Christ, but their own belly; and through smooth talk and blessing they deceive the hearts of the innocent.",
      "originalText": "For such do not serve our Lord Christ, but their own belly; and through smooth talk and blessing they deceive the hearts of the innocent.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.16.19",
      "sourceRef": "ROM.16.19",
      "sourceId": "blb.txt#line=28359",
      "sourceLabel": "19",
      "anchors": [
        "ROM.16.19"
      ],
      "mappingType": "exact",
      "text": "For your⁺ obedience has reached to all. Therefore I rejoice over you⁺. But I want you⁺ to be wise to good, and innocent to evil.",
      "originalText": "For your⁺ obedience has reached to all. Therefore I rejoice over you⁺. But I want you⁺ to be wise to good, and innocent to evil.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.16.20",
      "sourceRef": "ROM.16.20",
      "sourceId": "blb.txt#line=28360",
      "sourceLabel": "20",
      "anchors": [
        "ROM.16.20"
      ],
      "mappingType": "exact",
      "text": "And the God of peace will crush Satan under your⁺ feet in quickness. The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ [be] with you⁺.",
      "originalText": "And the God of peace will crush Satan under your⁺ feet in quickness. The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ [be] with you⁺.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.16.21",
      "sourceRef": "ROM.16.21",
      "sourceId": "blb.txt#line=28361",
      "sourceLabel": "21",
      "anchors": [
        "ROM.16.21"
      ],
      "mappingType": "exact",
      "text": "Timothy, my fellow worker, greets you⁺; [so] also Lucius and Jason and Sosipater, my kinsmen.",
      "originalText": "Timothy, my fellow worker, greets you⁺; [so] also Lucius and Jason and Sosipater, my kinsmen.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.16.22",
      "sourceRef": "ROM.16.22",
      "sourceId": "blb.txt#line=28362",
      "sourceLabel": "22",
      "anchors": [
        "ROM.16.22"
      ],
      "mappingType": "exact",
      "text": "I, Tertius, the one having written the letter, greet you⁺ in the Lord.",
      "originalText": "I, Tertius, the one having written the letter, greet you⁺ in the Lord.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.16.23",
      "sourceRef": "ROM.16.23",
      "sourceId": "blb.txt#line=28363",
      "sourceLabel": "23",
      "anchors": [
        "ROM.16.23"
      ],
      "mappingType": "exact",
      "text": "Gaius, the host of me and of the whole church, greets you⁺. Erastus the steward of the city greets you⁺; [so] also Quartus the brother.",
      "originalText": "Gaius, the host of me and of the whole church, greets you⁺. Erastus the steward of the city greets you⁺; [so] also Quartus the brother.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.16.25",
      "sourceRef": "ROM.16.25",
      "sourceId": "blb.txt#line=28365",
      "sourceLabel": "25",
      "anchors": [
        "ROM.16.25",
        "ROM.14.24"
      ],
      "mappingType": "relocated",
      "text": "Now to Him being able to strengthen you⁺ according to my gospel and the proclamation of Jesus Christ, according to the revelation of the mystery having been kept silent in the times of the ages,",
      "originalText": "Now to Him being able to strengthen you⁺ according to my gospel and the proclamation of Jesus Christ, according to the revelation of the mystery having been kept silent in the times of the ages,\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.16.26",
      "sourceRef": "ROM.16.26",
      "sourceId": "blb.txt#line=28366",
      "sourceLabel": "26",
      "anchors": [
        "ROM.16.26",
        "ROM.14.25"
      ],
      "mappingType": "relocated",
      "text": "but now having been made manifest also through the prophetic writings, according to the commandment of the eternal God having been made known to all the Gentiles unto obedience of faith—",
      "originalText": "but now having been made manifest also through the prophetic writings, according to the commandment of the eternal God having been made known to all the Gentiles unto obedience of faith—\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.16.27",
      "sourceRef": "ROM.16.27",
      "sourceId": "blb.txt#line=28367",
      "sourceLabel": "27",
      "anchors": [
        "ROM.16.27",
        "ROM.14.26"
      ],
      "mappingType": "relocated",
      "text": "[to] the only wise God [be] the glory unto the ages of the ages, which [is] through Jesus Christ! Amen.",
      "originalText": "[to] the only wise God [be] the glory unto the ages of the ages, which [is] through Jesus Christ! Amen."
    }
  ],
